====================================================================================
Profile-likelihood uncertainty on U, and what each Fisher estimator claimed
====================================================================================
  set            profile 1-sigma     AD Fisher     FD Fisher   AD error   FD error
  M         >          73.33 %        3845 %       2.217 %      52.4x       0.0x
  M+P+C              0.09547 %       0.075 %     0.07576 %       0.8x       0.8x

  The 'error' columns are each Fisher estimate divided by the likelihood answer.
  A Cramér–Rao value is a *lower* bound, so a ratio below 1 is mathematically
  legitimate -- but a ratio far below 1 means the bound is loose to the point of
  being misleading if it is read, as it usually is, as the achievable accuracy.
  A ratio above 1 is worse than loose: it is not a valid bound at all, and
  indicates the computed Fisher information is too small.
    - M: the AD bound EXCEEDS the measured uncertainty (52x), so it is not a valid bound. The minmod limiter
      zeroes derivative paths, making the computed information too small.
    - M: the FD bound is valid but loose by 33x -- the degeneracy is curved, and a Fisher
      matrix only ever sees local curvature.

  M vs M+P+C on U: at least 768x better with the full sensor set

